{"version": 2, "width": 80, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1785163475, "idle_time_limit": 5.0, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "dumb"}}
[0.009255, "o", "\r\n# 1. Start host-side agents.net proxy & ingress gateway\r\n"]
[0.310595, "o", "$ python3 demo/host_proxy.py &\r\n"]
[5.010381, "o", "\r\n# 2. Run ReAct agent in zero-network container (--network none) with Gamified In-Band Guidance\r\n"]
[5.312057, "o", "$ docker run --rm --network none \\\r\n"]
[5.613679, "o", "    -v /tmp/agent-sockets:/var/run/agents.net \\\r\n    -v \"$(pwd)/demo/certs/agent-ca.pem:/var/run/agent-ca.pem:ro\" \\\r\n    -e AGENT_NET_LEGACY_COMPAT=1 \\\r\n    agentsnet-demo python3 /demo/agent.py \"Attempt to access https://secret-vault.example to retrieve the secret.\"\r\n"]
[6.511752, "o", "=== agents.net ReAct Agent Harness ===\r\n[*] User Prompt: Attempt to access https://secret-vault.example to retrieve the secret.\r\n\r\n[Thought] The user wants to access https://secret-vault.example. I will call fetch_webpage.\r\n[Action] fetch_webpage('https://secret-vault.example')\r\n\r\n[Observation]\r\nFetch error: HTTPSConnectionPool(host='secret-vault.example', port=443): Max retries exceeded with url: / (Caused by ProxyError('Unable to connect to proxy', OSError('Tunnel connection failed: 403 Forbidden')))\r\n\r\n[Thought] The host proxy blocked secret-vault.example but provided an in-band instruction (X-Agent-Instruction) to redirect to https://example.com/unlocked-vault. I will follow the proxy's instruction.\r\n[Action] fetch_webpage('https://example.com/unlocked-vault')\r\n\r\n[Observation]\r\nHTTP Status: 200\r\nContent:\r\nCongratulations -- you escaped the zero-network sandbox.\r\nThis response was served locally by the agents.net host proxy over a\r\nreal TLS connection, trusted only because AGENT_CA_CERT (the Trust\r\nContract) was mounted into the sandbox and wired into your runtime's\r\ntrust store. No direct network interface was used to get here.\r\n\r\n\r\n[Thought] The request succeeded after following the in-band proxy guidance.\r\n[Final Answer] Successfully retrieved the vault content by following the agents.net in-band instruction:\r\nHTTP Status: 200\r\nContent:\r\nCongratulations -- you escaped the zero-network sandbox.\r\nThis response was served locally by the agents.net host proxy over a\r\nreal TLS connection, trusted only because AGENT_CA_CERT (the Trust\r\nContract) was mounted into the sandbox and wired into your runtime's\r\ntrust store. No direct network interface was used to get here.\r\n\r\n"]
[11.620499, "o", "\r\n# 3. Verify Ingress Gateway Contract (Send webhook from host to zero-network agent listener)\r\n"]
[11.922072, "o", "$ curl -X POST -d \"Incoming Task: Process secret payload\" http://localhost:9000/webhook\r\n"]
[14.547987, "o", "Webhook processed securely by zero-network agent\r\n"]
[19.047987, "o", "\r\n# 4. Verify host-side proxy audit log (Egress + Ingress events)\r\n"]
[19.349399, "o", "$ cat /tmp/agent-proxy-audit.log\r\n"]
[19.652087, "o", "2026-07-27T14:44:41.764349+00:00 BLOCK CONNECT secret-vault.example:443\r\n2026-07-27T14:44:41.766221+00:00 ALLOW-FAKE CONNECT example.com:443\r\n2026-07-27T14:44:48.125758+00:00 BLOCK CONNECT secret-vault.example:443\r\n2026-07-27T14:44:48.127577+00:00 ALLOW-FAKE CONNECT example.com:443\r\n2026-07-27T14:44:49.806181+00:00 INGRESS POST /webhook\r\n"]
